---
import GuidePage from '../../components/GuidePage.astro';
---

<GuidePage
  title="Add Fabric You Already Have"
  description="Measure project-local fat quarters, yardage, and remnants as the physical rectangles QuiltClarity can actually cut."
  eyebrow="Learn QuiltClarity · Existing fabric"
  guideSlug="add-fabric-you-have"
  guideCategory="start_here"
  previous={{ href: '/guides/enter-a-cut-list/', label: 'Enter a Cut List' }}
  next={{
    href: '/guides/check-pattern-yardage/',
    label: 'Check Pattern Yardage',
  }}
>
  <section>
    <h2>Measure each piece separately</h2><p>
      Across-fabric width runs from selvage side to selvage side; length runs
      with the fabric. A 12 × 20 remnant and an 8 × 20 remnant stay two bins,
      not one 20 × 20 area.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Presets are editable conveniences</h2><p>
      Fat quarter, fat eighth, quarter-yard, and half-yard actions fill common
      dimensions. Measure what you own and edit immediately. QuiltClarity plans
      the edited rectangle, not the preset label.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Quantity creates physical instances</h2><p>
      Quantity 2 means two separately identifiable pieces. Allocation results
      retain each instance so the cutting plan tells you which piece to use.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Safety applies only to purchases</h2><p>
      If the entered stock fits every cut, Buy now remains zero even when
      purchase safety is 5%. Safety cannot add margin to material already owned.
    </p>
  </section>
</GuidePage>
